<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<exercises xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ex_8_4">


<exercisegroup>
<title>Identifying Period, Amplitude, and Midline</title>
<introduction>
<p>
For each of the following, use a graph to identify the period, amplitude, and midline of the given function. Identify what transformations have been applied to either <m>f(t)=\cos(t)</m> or <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> to obtain the given function.
</p>
</introduction>

<exercise xml:id="exercise-8_4_1">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=5\cos(t)</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>2\pi</m>; amplitude: <m>5</m>; midline: <m>y=0</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\cos(t)</m> stretched vertically by a factor of <m>5</m>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=-4\sin(t)</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>2\pi</m>; amplitude: <m>4</m>; midline: <m>y=0</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> stretched vertically by a factor of <m>4</m> and reflected over the <m>t</m>-axis
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\sin\left(5t\right)</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period <m>\frac{2\pi}{5}</m>; amplitude: <m>1</m>; midline: <m>y=0</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> compressed horizontally by a factor of <m>5</m>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{3}t\right)</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>6</m>; amplitude: <m>1</m>; midline: <m>y=0</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\cos(t)</m> compressed horizontally by a factor of <m>\pi</m> and stretched horizontally by a factor of <m>3</m>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\cos(t)+10</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>2\pi</m>; amplitude: <m>1</m>; midline: <m>y=10</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\cos(t)</m> shifted up <m>10</m> units
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\sin(t)-6</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>2\pi</m>; amplitude: <m>1</m>; midline: <m>y=-6</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> shifted down <m>6</m> units
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\sin\left(\frac{3}{5}t\right)</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>\frac{10\pi}{3}</m>; amplitude: <m>1</m>; midline: <m>y=0</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> compressed horizontally by a factor of <m>3</m> and stretched horizontally by a factor of <m>5</m>
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=2\cos(t)-6</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>2\pi</m>; amplitude: <m>2</m>; midline: <m>y=-6</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\cos(t)</m> stretched vertically by a factor of <m>2</m> and shifted down <m>6</m> units
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=-3\sin(2t)</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>\pi</m>; amplitude: <m>3</m>; midline: <m>y=0</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> compressed horizontally by a factor of <m>2</m>, stretched vertically by a factor of <m>3</m>, and reflected over the <m>t</m>-axis
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>


<exercise xml:id="exercise-8_4_10">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=10\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{2}t\right)+4</m>
</p>
</statement>

<solution>
<p>
period: <m>4</m>; amplitude: <m>10</m>; midline: <m>y=4</m>. <m>y</m> is the graph of <m>f(t)=\sin(t)</m> compressed horizontally by a factor of <m>\pi</m>, stretched horizontally by a factor of <m>2</m>, stretched vertically by a factor of <m>10</m>, and shifted up <m>4</m> units
</p>
</solution>
</exercise>

</exercisegroup>


</exercises>
